.TH "REPROCTL\-DB" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-db \- database operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl db\f[R] \f[B]reset\f[R] [\f[B]\-y\f[R] |
\f[B]\(enyes\f[R]] | \f[B]migrate\f[R] | \f[B]shell\f[R] |
\f[B]status\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Perform database operations against the PostgreSQL instance running
inside the local cluster.
Tilt must be running for all subcommands.
.SS Subcommands
.TP
\f[B]reset\f[R] [\f[B]\-y\f[R] | \f[B]\(enyes\f[R]]
Drop and recreate the database.
This is only allowed from the main checkout, not from a worktree.
Prompts for confirmation unless \f[B]\-y\f[R] / \f[B]\(enyes\f[R] is
given.
.TP
\f[B]migrate\f[R]
Run any pending database migrations.
.TP
\f[B]shell\f[R]
Open an interactive \f[B]psql\f[R] session connected to the development
database.
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R]
Display connection information and the current migration state.
With the global \f[B]\(enjson\f[R] flag, outputs a JSON object with
host, port, database, and migration arrays (applied, pending, orphaned).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-y\f[R], \f[B]\(enyes\f[R]
Used with \f[B]reset\f[R].
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl db status
Show connection info and migration state.
.TP
reproctl \(enjson db status
Machine\-readable database and migration info.
.TP
reproctl db migrate
Apply pending migrations.
.TP
reproctl db shell
Open a psql session.
.TP
reproctl db reset \-y
Drop and recreate without confirmation.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-start\f[R](1)
.SH AUTHORS
Repro.
